{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Declared mutants of v8-framework-shell (docs/framework/architecture.md, Design Invariant 6; docs/architecture/plans/framework-rework/shell-sketch.md). Run with docs/architecture/plans/time-threads-trace/scripts/run_mutations.py --catalog docs/architecture/plans/framework-rework/scripts/framework_shell_mutations.json --build-dir <a tree with BUILD_TESTING=ON, the SDL renderer and ImGui>. The window and ImGui checks run through run_shell_test.py, which sets SDL's dummy video driver, the software renderer and the working directory as tests/framework/CMakeLists.txt does for CTest. fw-shell-argv-raw is killed by H3 on macOS and Linux and by H1 on Windows. Known limits without a mutant: the console guard of RunHeadlessShell cannot be observed on POSIX; removing Clear or Present is not detected. A mutant is killed only when its check fails with the expected message. The fw-close-* mutants (v8-framework-close-request, docs/tools/plans/v8/model-viewer.md) check Q1-Q3.",
  "mutants": [
    {
      "id": "fw-shell-argv-raw",
      "what": "The headless shell passes argv on instead of Engine's UTF-8 command line (macOS and Linux: H3; Windows: H1)",
      "file": "framework/src/HeadlessShell.cpp",
      "find": "    const auto commandLine = Engine::Os::Console::CommandLineUtf8(argc, argv);\n    if (!commandLine) {\n        const std::string reason = Engine::Base::Describe(commandLine.error());\n        return failure(reason);\n    }\n    return body(std::span<const std::string>(commandLine.value()));",
      "replace": "    static_cast<void>(failure);\n    const std::vector<std::string> arguments(argv, argv + argc);\n    return body(std::span<const std::string>(arguments));",
      "target": "gyo_framework_tests",
      "cases": "H*",
      "expect": "is NOT correct"
    },
    {
      "id": "fw-shell-failure-code",
      "what": "A command line with no UTF-8 form returns 2 instead of the failure function's value",
      "file": "framework/src/HeadlessShell.cpp",
      "find": "        return failure(reason);",
      "replace": "        static_cast<void>(failure(reason));\n        return 2;",
      "target": "gyo_framework_tests",
      "cases": "H*",
      "expect": "is NOT correct"
    },
    {
      "id": "fw-shell-body-code",
      "what": "The headless shell returns 0 instead of the body's value",
      "file": "framework/src/HeadlessShell.cpp",
      "find": "    return body(std::span<const std::string>(commandLine.value()));",
      "replace": "    static_cast<void>(body(std::span<const std::string>(commandLine.value())));\n    return 0;",
      "target": "gyo_framework_tests",
      "cases": "H*",
      "expect": "is NOT correct"
    },
    {
